      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.047,
            0.419,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.093,
            0.847,
            0.159
          ],
          "content": "Explaining this in a different way: To express $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ as a percentage, we need to find its equivalent fraction with 100 as the denominator. Two ways of going ahead are shown below."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.175,
            0.344,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": "Method 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.585,
            0.175,
            0.688,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "Method 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.205,
            0.385,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} &= \\frac{3 \\times 25}{4 \\times 25} \\\\&= \\frac{75}{100} = 75\\%\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.52,
            0.206,
            0.753,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} &= \\frac{x}{100} \\cdot \\\\\\frac{3}{4} \\times 100 &= \\frac{x}{100} \\times 100 \\\\\\left[  multiply both sides by   100 \\right] \\\\x &= \\frac{3}{4} \\times 100 \\\\&= 75.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.342,
            0.45,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ can be expressed as 75%."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.371,
            0.845,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": "Observe the following bar model diagram showing the equivalence between $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ and 75%."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.431,
            0.776,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_chart_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.662,
            0.805,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": "Can you tell what percentage of the colour was made using yellow?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.705,
            0.846,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 2:** Surya won some prize money in a contest. He wants to save $\\frac { 2 } { 5 }$ of the money to purchase a new canvas. Express this quantity as a percentage."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.774,
            0.846,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": "Try to understand the different methods for solving this problem, as shown below."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.828,
            0.407,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "\\operatorname { M e t h o d 1 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.859,
            0.415,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} &= \\frac{20}{50} = \\frac{40}{100} \\\\&= 40\\%.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.56,
            0.827,
            0.719,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} & 故  \\; \\begin{aligned}\\\\ &\\bmod 2 \\\\&\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{x}{100}.\\\\ &\\end{aligned}\\\\ &\\quad x = \\frac{2}{5} \\times 100 = 40.\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.913,
            0.114,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": "2"
        }
      ]
    }
